# Since the ".env" file is gitignored, you can use the ".env.example" file to
# build a new ".env" file when you clone the repo. Keep this file up-to-date
# when you add new variables to `.env`.

# This file will be committed to version control, so make sure not to have any
# secrets in it. If you are cloning this repo, create a copy of this file named
# ".env" and populate it with your secrets.

# When adding additional environment variables, the schema in "/src/env.js"
# should be updated accordingly.

# Optional: OpenAI key for the Ask chat. Without it, plain-English search still works.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=""

# Optional: HTTP(S) proxy with a Korean egress IP so the Naver source works.
# Naver Land drops packets from non-Korean and datacenter IPs (even Vercel Seoul/icn1),
# so without a proxy the Naver chip fails soft and only Zigbang and Peterpan load.
# Any standard HTTP CONNECT proxy works: a Korean residential/mobile proxy provider,
# or e.g. tinyproxy/squid on a home network or KT/SKT/LG U+ connection in Korea.
# NAVER_PROXY_URL="http://user:pass@host:port"

# Optional alternative: Bright Data Web Unlocker (https://brightdata.com).
# Naver API calls are sent through their REST endpoint with country=kr;
# billing is per successful request. NAVER_PROXY_URL wins when both are set.
# BRIGHTDATA_API_KEY=""
# BRIGHTDATA_UNLOCKER_ZONE="web_unlocker1"

# Optional: set SKIP_ENV_VALIDATION=1 for Docker/CI builds.
